{"actor":"literature","data":{"citation":{"first_author":"Md Ahsanul Tarafder","identifier":"doi:10.2139/ssrn.6455598","title":"Improving Loan Default Prediction Using Class Imbalance Techniques: A Comparative Study of SMOTE and Class Weighting Methods","year":2026},"claim":"Class weighting in logistic regression achieved a significantly higher recall (0.66) compared to SMOTE (0.17) in a loan default prediction scenario.","concepts":["class imbalance","oversampling","class weight","logistic regression","recall"],"id":"E1","quote":"The application of SMOTE improved recall to 0.17, while the class-weighted Logistic Regression model significantly increased recall to 0.66.","stance":"supports"},"hash":"5696b4c98830192abfbfd62e8c012223f36fb58dee40e919d84ff95c81af3eb2","kind":"artefact","prev":"1232f40dc650c2481ee0f9f15861d744cfb5207bf76adda3f552e9771dee6a46","seq":12,"stage":"evidence","ts":"2026-10-10T06:03:14.064+00:00"}
{"actor":"literature","data":{"citation":{"first_author":"Erick Cheruiyot Kirui","identifier":"doi:10.61440/jems.2026.v1.05","title":"Predicting Neonatal Mortality Using Demographic and Health Survey Data: Comparing Logistic Regression and Machine Learning under Severe Class Imbalance","year":2026},"claim":"When using logistic regression with SMOTE (oversampling), recall reaches 0.712, which is higher than the class-weighted logistic regression model in other contexts, though precision is very low.","concepts":["class imbalance","oversampling","class weight","logistic regression","recall"],"id":"E2","quote":"LR+SMOTE leads on recall (0.712) and ROC-AUC (0.861) but with very low precision (0.025).","stance":"supports"},"hash":"d6f426223de0e4b1e5bdde88de2029df73aec5f5cb3248e705fba63d265dacfd","kind":"artefact","prev":"5696b4c98830192abfbfd62e8c012223f36fb58dee40e919d84ff95c81af3eb2","seq":13,"stage":"evidence","ts":"2026-10-10T06:03:14.065+00:00"}
