{"actor":"hypothesis","data":{"concepts":["generalizability","model family","dataset scope"],"description":"The evidence only compares SMOTE (random oversampling) and class weighting in logistic regression within a single dataset and specific use case—loan default prediction. This limits generalizability to other imbalanced binary classification problems or different model families.","evidence_ids":["E1"],"id":"G1","kind":"narrow_scope"},"hash":"2bc0c6e72f7ddf0e9257442611b3c6a3fcc857fc009efcb65ae1745a57e3b178","kind":"artefact","prev":"e83403ff225f156f40f2e5f03fbfa8ec5cb3a6bca81fd3b5ea78264f71a1647c","seq":19,"stage":"gaps","ts":"2026-10-10T06:03:14.065+00:00"}
{"actor":"hypothesis","data":{"concepts":["alternative_oversampling_methods","alternative_models"],"description":"The study does not evaluate other oversampling techniques (e.g., ADASYN, borderline SMOTE) or alternative classifiers (e.g., XGBoost, random forests) that may perform better with oversampling, so the comparison is restricted to only logistic regression and class weighting.","evidence_ids":["E1"],"id":"G2","kind":"narrow_scope"},"hash":"6486db3ab153d30cde057ac3bb7bb6653f71a029b0a8aa7e1d63125873f8f9a1","kind":"artefact","prev":"2bc0c6e72f7ddf0e9257442611b3c6a3fcc857fc009efcb65ae1745a57e3b178","seq":20,"stage":"gaps","ts":"2026-10-10T06:03:14.065+00:00"}
