{"actor":"hypothesis","data":{"dependent_variable":"minority-class recall","evidence_ids":["E1"],"expected_direction":"increase","gap_ids":["G1","G2","G3","G4"],"id":"H1","independent_variable":"oversampling method (SMOTE vs. class weighting)","rationale":"This hypothesis directly challenges the claim in E1 that class weighting achieves significantly higher recall (0.66 vs. 0.17), and aims to test generalizability across datasets and model contexts. It addresses G1 (narrow scope), G2 (limited methods), and G4 (lack of statistical validation) by proposing a falsifiable outcome under broader conditions.","statement":"In imbalanced binary classification tasks on public tabular datasets, random oversampling (e.g., SMOTE) will achieve a higher minority-class recall than class weighting in logistic regression."},"hash":"3286f7b6fc15c77d52b4673c1f036d6d17c8cd3761d9872a3225415294404ff8","kind":"artefact","prev":"cec5a2eccb5ee9185196ba08e83db5612d741b0609c14fb3fd7e60ae3ea1c548","seq":24,"stage":"hypotheses","ts":"2026-10-10T06:03:14.066+00:00"}
{"actor":"hypothesis","data":{"dependent_variable":"F1-score","evidence_ids":["E1"],"expected_direction":"increase","gap_ids":["G2","G3"],"id":"H2","independent_variable":"oversampling method (ADASYN, borderline SMOTE, SMOTE, class weighting)","rationale":"This hypothesis targets G2 (lack of alternative methods) and G3 (missing F1-score evaluation). It introduces a more comprehensive comparison across methods and metrics, enabling evaluation of performance beyond recall and improving the practical utility of the findings.","statement":"In imbalanced binary classification, the use of alternative oversampling methods (e.g., ADASYN, borderline SMOTE) in combination with logistic regression leads to higher F1-score than class weighting or standard SMOTE."},"hash":"010d4031016fbe7c63ae10d5be75596919cfe7988fc3712a52fc96a902277d2d","kind":"artefact","prev":"3286f7b6fc15c77d52b4673c1f036d6d17c8cd3761d9872a3225415294404ff8","seq":25,"stage":"hypotheses","ts":"2026-10-10T06:03:14.066+00:00"}
