{"actor":"experiment","data":{"evidence_ids":["E1"],"hypothesis_id":"H1","id":"K1","limitations":["The comparison is limited to two datasets and one model (logistic regression), restricting generalizability beyond these specific conditions.","The effect size in breast_cancer_imb10 is minimal (dz = 0.023), while in digits_binary_imb10 it is large but in the opposite direction (dz = -0.683), indicating inconsistent outcomes.","The control condition in E1 (0.66 vs. 0.17) is not directly replicable here, as the actual recall values in the experiments are much lower, suggesting a potential mismatch in experimental setup or dataset conditions."],"result_id":"R1","statement":"In the breast_cancer_imb10 dataset, the minority recall difference between oversampling (0.026) and class weighting (0.025) is negligible (mean_diff = 0.0012, p = 0.6547), while in digits_binary_imb10, oversampling yields a lower recall (0.024) than class weighting (0.042) (mean_diff = -0.0185, p = 0.0253). The Holm-adjusted p-value for the primary metric remains above 0.05 (p_holm = 0.0507), failing to establish a statistically significant difference under the hypothesis's expected direction.","verdict":"inconclusive"},"hash":"fe940e02d1db6a41fd8ee6154180a928af259a831fa0a2b0866e85f6c7d56a12","kind":"artefact","prev":"b628d0d69ce3663da1dd3b7ab77863cc5cb0fe4e5279d66bd63c6b736de68ff2","seq":54,"stage":"conclusion","ts":"2026-10-10T06:03:14.576+00:00"}
